# made of 6c23f7ccacae8df1
# the allocation of a literal lists the stores that stand right behind it, and a store that lays what the slot of a fresh object holds is not built. The answers turn on the order of the keys, on who sees the object in between, and on a store of another value of the same kind
# f2 = make, f5 = makeSeen, f6 = makeOver, f7 = makeSame
# RUN(FORM): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# FORM-LABEL: code f2:Body
# FORM: = NewObject {{*}}fields=[1, 0, 2]
# RUN(SEEN): walk f5 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# SEEN-LABEL: code f5:Body
# SEEN: = NewObject {{*}}fields=[1]
# RUN(OVER): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# OVER-LABEL: code f6:Body
# OVER: = PutSlot {{*}}key="count"
# OVER: = PutSlot {{*}}key="name"
# RUN(SAME): walk f7 mechanisms=all
# SAME-NOT: key="count"
# SAME-NOT: key="name"
